# Nested Flows

## Overview

A Flow module used in a DSL `step` becomes a canonical Flow call. This is the
only implicit child Flow derivation.

Run the cells from top to bottom.

## Install The Package

```elixir
Mix.install([{:jido_action, "~> 3.0.0-beta.11"}])
```

## Define A Child Flow

```elixir
defmodule NestedFlows.AddOne do
  use Jido.Action, name: "nested_flows_add_one"

  @impl true
  def run(%{value: value}, _context), do: {:ok, %{value: value + 1}}
end

defmodule NestedFlows.Child do
  use Jido.Flow, name: "nested_flows_child"

  flow do
    step "add",
      action: NestedFlows.AddOne,
      params: %{value: input(:value)}

    output(%{value: result("add", :value)})
  end
end
```

## Use The Child In A Step

```elixir
defmodule NestedFlows.Parent do
  use Jido.Flow, name: "nested_flows_parent"

  flow do
    step "child",
      action: NestedFlows.Child,
      params: %{value: input(:value)}

    step "finish",
      action: NestedFlows.AddOne,
      params: %{value: result("child", :value)}

    output(%{value: result("finish", :value)})
  end
end
```

```elixir
%{
  kind: :call,
  call: {%Jido.Instruction{kind: :flow, target: NestedFlows.Child}, _params}
} = NestedFlows.Parent.flow().components["child"]

{:ok, %{value: 3}} =
  Jido.Exec.run(NestedFlows.Parent, %{value: 1})
```

The DSL shape stays `step ... action: ChildFlow`. The lowerer stores an inert
Flow Instruction template in the call node.

## Native Execution Boundary

A Subflow lowers to a nested native Runic Workflow. Step-wise execution can
show child validators, child Steps, InputBinding, and connection work. Jido
does not hide these native runnables.

The child inherits the parent context, `max_concurrency`, `task_supervisor` routing, and
execution ID. Its Action calls share the parent execution budget.

Child output uses the same caller context as root Flow output. This includes
context references inside expressions, maps, and lists. Input references read
the validated child input. Result references read components in that child.
A missing context key returns a reference error. A key with a `nil` value is
present and resolves to `nil`. These rules also apply to managed Runic execution.

An Action failure keeps its typed error and leaf details. Its
`details.node_path` identifies the authored Subflow path, for example
`["child", "add"]`. Child input and output validation failures identify the
Subflow boundary instead, for example `["child"]`. Errors before Action
validation can lack this path. See
[Read Failures](https://github.com/agentjido/jido_action/blob/release/v3/guides/debugging-flows.md#read-failures)
for single and concurrent failure inspection.

## Limits

Only `step` derives Subflow. Choice options, Choice fallback, Map, Reduce, and
Iterate target slots require Actions. A canonical child call stores a Flow
module, not an arbitrary runtime Flow value.

Validate the complete boundary without running work:

```elixir
Jido.Exec.compile(NestedFlows.Parent)
```
